  "definition": "Attitude control changes or maintains a spacecraft's orientation. A guidance function supplies the desired orientation, attitude determination estimates the current one, and a controller commands actuators to reduce the error. This loop supports payload pointing, communications, thermal management and solar-array illumination while rejecting disturbances such as aerodynamic drag, gravity-gradient torque and solar radiation pressure.[^1][^3]",
